  "customimagePath": "Background Source",
  "customimagePathTipTitle": "Enter a custom background using one of these formats",
  "customimagePathTipToggle": "View instructions",
  "customimagePathTip": "1. Relative path in the assets folder<br>e.g. assets/image.png or url(assets/image.png)<br>2. Web image URL<br>e.g. https://picsum.photos/1920/1080 or url(https://picsum.photos/1920/1080)<br>3. CSS function<br>e.g. linear-gradient(to right in oklch, #f59e0b, #06b6d4 66%, #6366f1)<br>4. Solid color<br>e.g. red, #06b6d4, oklch(from blue calc(l + 0.1) c h), color-mix(in hsl, #f59e0b, transparent)<br>5. Combine any of the above, separated by commas<br>e.g. repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent, transparent 20px, oklch(60% 0.2 10 / 0.15) 20px, oklch(60% 0.2 10 / 0.15) 40px), #8effce",
  "customimageAsset": "Resources",
  "customimageAssetPickerFailed": "Resource file selection failed",
  "customimageBasicParams": "Basic Settings",
  "customimageZLevel": "Layer",
  "customimageZLevelTip": "The layer controls the position of the background texture relative to the content layer (editing area)<br>1. Backdrop: the background texture is behind the content layer; in this state the content layer opacity can be adjusted additionally<br>2. Content: the background texture is on the same level as the content layer<br>3. Topmost: the background texture overlays the entire page",
  "customimageZLevelBackdrop": "Backdrop",
  "customimageZLevelContent": "Content",
  "customimageZLevelTopmost": "Topmost",
  "customimageLayoutOpacity": "Content Opacity",
  "customimageLayoutOpacityTip": "When the layer is Backdrop, the background texture is behind the content layer (editing area)<br>The lower the content opacity value, the more visible the background texture is in the editing area",
  "customimageEffect": "Blend Mode",
  "customimageEffectTip": "Blend mode determines how the background texture blends with the page background color<br>You may need to adjust opacity when changing the blend mode<br>1. Normal: the texture is displayed as-is without blending<br>2. Multiply: colors are multiplied, darkening the result, good for light textures<br>3. Screen: the inverse of multiply, brightening the result, good for dark textures<br>4. Overlay: darkens shadows and brightens highlights to increase contrast<br>5. Soft Light: similar to overlay but softer<br>6. Color: keeps the background brightness and applies the texture hue and saturation<br>7. Luminosity: keeps the background hue and saturation and applies the texture brightness<br>8. Color Burn: darkens the background, more noticeable with darker textures<br>9. Color Dodge: lightens the background, more noticeable with brighter textures",
  "customimageEffectNormal": "Normal",
  "customimageEffectMultiply": "Multiply",
  "customimageEffectLuminosity": "Luminosity",
  "customimageEffectScreen": "Screen",
  "customimageEffectColor": "Color",
  "customimageEffectOverlay": "Overlay",
  "customimageEffectSoftLight": "Soft Light",
  "customimageEffectColorBurn": "Color Burn",
  "customimageEffectColorDodge": "Color Dodge",
  "customimageFillMode": "Fill Mode",
  "customimageFillModeTip": "Fill mode determines how the background texture is placed on the page<br>1. Scale to Cover: scales the texture to fill the background while preserving its proportions, cropping any overflow<br>2. Tile: repeats the texture across the background at its original size<br>3. Custom: manually set the width and height of the texture, with an option to repeat it",
